{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterReflectionCocycle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterReflectionCocycle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolicCoset","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Inversion","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.length_minRep_mul_wordProd'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.length_minRep_mul_wordProd'","kind":"theorem","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L478-L486","doc":"**The Bourbaki lifting lemma, UNCONDITIONAL**: a minimal coset\nrepresentative `u` and a reduced `J`-word `p` satisfy\n`ℓ(u · π p) = ℓ(u) + |p|` — at every rank, from Mathlib's primitives\nalone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.rightExchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.rightExchange","kind":"theorem","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L464-L473","doc":"**The right exchange property holds in every Coxeter system** — the\nhypothesis of the parabolic-coset lifting lemma, discharged\nunconditionally. This closes the audited Mathlib gap: the braid and\nfar-commutation coset reductions no longer rest on an unproved\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.strong_exchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.strong_exchange","kind":"theorem","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L456-L462","doc":"**STRONG EXCHANGE** (Bjorner–Brenti Thm 1.4.3): if `t` is a right\ninversion of `π ω` — any reflection, any word, reducedness NOT required —\nthen `π ω · t` is obtained by deleting a single letter of `ω`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:coxeter-strong-exchange","label":"prop:coxeter-strong-exchange","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/coxeter-strong-exchange.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_eq_one_of_isRightInversion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_eq_one_of_isRightInversion","kind":"theorem","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L430-L454","doc":"**The key equivalence direction**: a right inversion has `η = 1` —\nby the self-inverse trick `η(wt, t) = η(t, t) + η(w, t) = 1 + η(w, t)`:\nwere `η(w, t) = 0`, a reduced word for `w t` would delete a letter and\ngive `ℓ(w) < ℓ(w t)`, contradicting `ℓ(w t) < ℓ(w)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.length_mul_lt_of_eta_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.length_mul_lt_of_eta_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L420-L428","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.exists_eraseIdx_of_eta_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.exists_eraseIdx_of_eta_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L410-L418","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.mem_rightInvSeq_of_eta_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.mem_rightInvSeq_of_eta_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L404-L408","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_isReflection_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_isReflection_self","kind":"theorem","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L365-L400","doc":"**`η(t, t) = 1` for every reflection `t`** — the three-line cocycle\nalgebra (no induction): decompose `t = w σ_c w⁻¹` and expand `η(t, t)`\nwith the cocycle law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_inv_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_inv_add","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L360-L363","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_simple_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_simple_self","kind":"theorem","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L354-L358","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_one","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L350-L352","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_mul","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L337-L348","doc":"**The cocycle law**: `η(uv, t) = η(v, t) + η(u, v t v⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.etaHom_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.etaHom_apply","kind":"theorem","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L332-L335","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_wordProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta_wordProd","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L327-L330","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.eta","kind":"def","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L321-L325","doc":"The reflection cocycle `η(w, t) ∈ ℤ/2` — for `w = π ω`, the parity of\nthe number of occurrences of `t` in the right inversion sequence of `ω`,\nwell-defined on `W` (word-independent) because it is computed through the\nhomomorphism `etaHom`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.etaHom_wordProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.etaHom_wordProd","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L315-L319","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.etaHom_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.etaHom_simple","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L312-L313","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.etaHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.etaHom","kind":"def","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L307-L310","doc":"The cocycle representation `W →* Perm (W × ℤ/2)`, via the universal\nproperty of the Coxeter presentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocyclePerm_liftable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocyclePerm_liftable","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L280-L303","doc":"**The cocycle permutations satisfy the Coxeter relations.** The parity\ncount over the inversion sequence of the doubled braid word vanishes\nbecause the sequence is two identical halves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocyclePerm_mul_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocyclePerm_mul_pow","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L271-L278","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.getElem_leftInvSeq_alternatingWord_period","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.getElem_leftInvSeq_alternatingWord_period","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L256-L267","doc":"**Period-`m` structure of the inversion sequence of the braid word**:\nentry `k + m` equals entry `k`, by `(σⱼ σᵢ)^{M i j} = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.wordProd_alternatingWord_odd_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.wordProd_alternatingWord_odd_add","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L245-L254","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.wordProd_alternatingWord_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.wordProd_alternatingWord_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L237-L243","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.alternatingWord_two_mul_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.alternatingWord_two_mul_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L227-L235","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.alternatingWord_odd_succ_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.alternatingWord_odd_succ_succ","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L220-L225","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.alternatingWord_two_mul_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.alternatingWord_two_mul_succ","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L213-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleWord_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleWord_apply","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L176-L209","doc":"**The master formula**: the composite cocycle permutation of a word\n`ω` conjugates by `π ω` and adds the ℤ/2 count of `t` in the right\ninversion sequence of `ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleWord_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleWord_cons","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L172-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleWord_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleWord_nil","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L170-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleWord","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L166-L168","doc":"The composite cocycle permutation of a word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocyclePerm_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocyclePerm_apply","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L163-L164","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocyclePerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocyclePerm","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L159-L161","doc":"The cocycle step as a permutation of `W × ℤ/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleFun_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleFun_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L135-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cocycleFun","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L130-L133","doc":"The reflection-cocycle step at generator `i`:\n`(w, ε) ↦ (σᵢ w σᵢ, ε + [w = σᵢ])`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_eq_zero_of_period","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_eq_zero_of_period","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L96-L118","doc":"A list of length `2m` whose entries repeat with period `m` has every\nparity count zero: the list is two equal halves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.mem_of_parityCount_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.mem_of_parityCount_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L84-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_reverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_reverse","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L80-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_append","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L76-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_cons","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L72-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount_nil","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.parityCount","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterReflectionCocycle.lean#L66-L68","doc":"The ℤ/2 parity of the number of occurrences of `t` in `l`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}